            "review_title": "Review at My Mother Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Paul M\nTexas Gulf Coast, Texas14 contributions\n0\nElegant food at reasonable price\nDec 2017 • Couples\nThis restaurant as been open about 9 days. It has more of a French feel than Vietnamese. The food is the best I've had in Saigon. Wonderful flavor profile, portions were correct. Enough where you wanted 1 or 2 more bites but feeling satisfied and not full. The chef took traditional Vietnamese food to a new level. There were also very nice deserts. The distance between table and chairs is also good.There is also outdoors seating which allows smoking and indoors is non smoking. The only weak point is wait staff is still trying to get their rhythm bit not a problem. I complemented the food to the owner and he introduced me to the chef. A Vietnamese women who has been professionally trained and cooking for over 30 years. The owner is a Vietnamese man who is well educated and traveled. I 'am taking some couples out for a dinner celebration and this is where I will take them.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 7, 2018",
